  "title": "Conference of the Birds (Mantiq al-Tayr)",
  "summary": "The Mantiq al-Tayr (Language of the Birds, Conference of the Birds) is a Sufi parable in verse by the Persian poet Farid al-Din Attar of Nishapur, about the desire for union with God. Attar gives 573/1177 as its completion year, though that verse is missing from some manuscripts and the Met dates it about 1187.",
